-- title:
--   Gauss valuations: residue degree bound and uniqueness at equality
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a principal ideal domain with fraction field $K_0$, and let $F$ be a field that is an algebra over both $R$ and $K_0$, compatibly (a scalar tower). Let $j \in F$ be transcendental over $R$, and assume $F$ is finite-dimensional and separable over the intermediate field $K_0(j)$ generated by $j$. Let $\varpi \in R$ be a prime element and let $V$ be a valuation subring of $F$ such that the image of $R$ in $F$ lies in $V$, the image of $\varpi$ lies in the non-units of $V$, and for every polynomial $P \in R[X]$ not divisible by the constant polynomial $\varpi$ both $P(j)$ and $P(j)^{-1}$ lie in $V$ (a Gauss-type condition). Let $\mathbb{F}$ be a field receiving a surjective algebra map from $R$, equipped with an algebra structure on the residue field $\kappa(V)$ of the local ring $V$ such that for every $r \in R$ the image of $r$ in $\mathbb{F}$, mapped into $\kappa(V)$, equals the residue of $r \in V$; finally let $jV \in V$ be an element whose image in $F$ is $j$. The conclusion has three parts: $\kappa(V)$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield $\mathbb{F}(\overline{j})$ generated by the residue $\overline{j}$ of $jV$; its degree is at most $\operatorname{finrank}_{K_0(j)} F$; and, should the opposite inequality $\operatorname{finrank}_{K_0(j)} F \le [\kappa(V) : \mathbb{F}(\overline{j})]$ also hold, then every non-unit $f$ of $V$ satisfies $f\varpi^{-1} \in V$ (so the maximal ideal of $V$ is generated by $\varpi$), and $V$ is the unique valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $R$, with $\varpi$ a non-unit, and satisfying the same Gauss-type condition for $j$.
--
--   This is the comparison of the residue degree of a Gauss-type valuation of a function field with the degree of the function field over the rational subfield $K_0(j)$, together with the statement that equality forces the valuation to be unramified over the prime $\varpi$ and uniquely determined; it is the valuation-theoretic input for reduction of curves given by two charts. It is used in [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.isDomain_tensorProduct_chartAlg_of_finrank_le_finrank_adjoin_range`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.isDomain_tensorProduct_chartAlg_of_finrank_le_finrank_adjoin_range), and its proof invokes the discreteness of localisations of height-one primes of an integrally closed Noetherian domain and the fundamental identity for primes of an integral closure over a discrete valuation ring.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_finrank_residueField_le_and_forall_mul_inv_mem_and_forall_eq_of_gauss.lean

